From: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: power the core down when probe fails

Probe powers the core up with pm_runtime_get_sync() before loading the
firmware. When that or anything after it failed, the error path dropped
the usage count with pm_runtime_put_noidle() and marked the device
suspended, so the runtime suspend callback never ran and the core,
bus and vcodec clocks stayed on. On the watch those are XO-fed GCC
branches, and with no firmware found at boot they kept the SoC out of
XO shutdown for good.

Suspend the core on the way out when the get had succeeded.

Signed-off-by: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -451,11 +451,11 @@ static int venus_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ret = pm_runtime_get_sync(dev);
 	if (ret < 0)
-		goto err_runtime_disable;
+		goto err_runtime_put;
 
 	ret = venus_firmware_init(core);
 	if (ret)
-		goto err_runtime_disable;
+		goto err_runtime_suspend;
 
 	ret = venus_boot(core);
 	if (ret)
@@ -515,8 +515,16 @@ static int venus_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	venus_shutdown(core);
 err_firmware_deinit:
 	venus_firmware_deinit(core);
-err_runtime_disable:
+err_runtime_suspend:
+	/*
+	 * The get above powered the core up. Marking it suspended alone would
+	 * leave its clocks on, and the SoC never reaching XO shutdown.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_put_sync_suspend(dev);
+	goto err_runtime_disable;
+err_runtime_put:
 	pm_runtime_put_noidle(dev);
+err_runtime_disable:
 	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
 	pm_runtime_set_suspended(dev);
 	v4l2_device_unregister(&core->v4l2_dev);
-- 
2.43.0
